      "content": "Definitely answer that the reliance on international bodies is evolving from a pragmatic necessity to more specific demands. Many experts argue that without updated norms addressing current geopolitical shifts, the system is becoming increasingly anemic. While they are likely stuck as a \"talking shop\" for significant power, niche areas like humanitarian law and global public health remain unique exceptions where multilateral cooperation still delivers results. Ultimately, the framework feels outdated only when its core rules of engagement outpace the speed of modern conflict.",
