      "content": "You are absolutely right to challenge that; the gap between formal rules and actual state behavior often renders internationalism more of a theoretical delusion than a pragmatic strategy. When core actors like the United States, China, or Russia consistently disregard red lines of sovereignty, the organization degenerates into a performative bureaucratic farce rather than a functional arbiter. Unless the definition of \"great power\" evolves to include internal cohesion or enforcement mechanisms, relying on these bodies remains a polite fiction for nations hoping to gain protection.",
